WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.168
Welcome back to our program.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:05.305
So what are the questions you have today?

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.072
Are there

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.873
actually still

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.143
more questions than answers?

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.311
Oh, absolutely.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.513
There are more questions than answers.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.749
I think the first question on my mind

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.951
is, was promotion alone

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:19.853
or were people

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:20.820
in the Kremlin

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.554
or in Moscow

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.623
actually supporting his efforts

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:27.060
as a way to weaken Putin inside Russia,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.362
something we don't know anything about?

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.264
We don't know where Prigozhin is.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.500
We don't know where Putin is.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.168
We are still watching

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.070
what the next steps will be.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.873
It is hard to imagine that Putin

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.342
will accept this attack on his leadership

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.411
without repercussions

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.145
of some kind,

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.614
going after him, trying to kill Prigozhin

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.481
and Prigozhin,

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.482
anticipating

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.850
that is going to

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.752
have protected himself somewhere

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.954
and be planning what he can do as well.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.723
Ultimately,

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.858
and I hate to keep going on here,

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.693
but this is about the narrative.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.328
This is about what they're telling

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.863
the Russian people.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.633
Prigozhin wants to be seen as a hero,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.802
as a savior of Russia,

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.336
that the people leading Russia

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.172
were leading them astray.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:15.008
And Putin wants to be seen also

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.844
as the savior of Russia against a mutiny.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.213
So that's why they are doing this dance

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.515
really off screen right now

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.118
to see how they can position themselves

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.619
about where this goes next.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.888
Can I just pick up on what you said?

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.057
It would be interesting to know how much

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.258
support promotion

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.527
had from within the establishment.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.696
I mean, clearly not enough.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.331
Otherwise you wouldn't have turned around

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.934
Well well, first off,

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.168
the amount of support

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.871
he had is really striking.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.973
He took over the military base

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.641
in Rostov on Don

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:51.277
the military base in Baton Rouge

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.013
and did so without firing a shot.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.915
He had people in the streets

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.017
bringing flowers and bread and water

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.119
And so

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.454
there was clearly a show of support

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.990
for promotion in doing this.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.693
And everybody else

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.561
who should have been on Putin's team

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.597
here was just kind of sitting it out.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:11.698
Some were even getting on

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:12.799
their airplanes.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.001
So it showed a relative weakness for

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:19.139
a relative or worse promotion.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:21.107
That is really striking.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.842
He may not have accumulated

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.110
the forces that he wanted

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.146
to be able to take Moscow,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.247
but he showed that

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.615
he actually has

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.817
some residents in the Russian military

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.252
and the Russian population.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.853
So let me ask you then,

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.121
what the United States

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.189
should do about this.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:37.323
Is the president was very clear

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.791
and actually all weekend,

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.527
none of the NATO allies came out

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.529
with anything much more then.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.030
We're watching the situation.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.865
We're talking to our partners.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:46.566
They obviously didn't

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.601
want to give any excuse to

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.270
anybody like the foreign minister.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.071
Lavrov already has

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.206
said that investigation

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.208
will will commence on on on

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:57.577
whether the West was involved in this.

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:59.646
We heard what President Biden said today.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.515
What would next from the U.S.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.750
perspective and from the

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.817
NATO's perspective?

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.221
Well, first several things.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:08.888
First off,

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:11.791
I think it's important to make clear,

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.358
as President

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.660
Biden has done, as Secretary

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.994
Blinken has done,

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.863
that we have nothing to do with this.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:19.032
There will be efforts to blame the West

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.067
and we should preempt them by saying

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.735
we had nothing to do with this.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:25.071
This is an internal Russian thing.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.172
The second thing is

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.208
we should drop the restrictions on

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.642
aid to Ukraine.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.612
The Russian soldiers sitting in trenches

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.280
in Ukraine right now

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.982
do not want to be there.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.650
They know that their country

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.652
is coming apart behind them.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.387
They know the imperial quest

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.288
that Putin has set

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.423
them on is failing

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:45.391
and they don't want to be there.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.559
So we should be giving

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.061
Ukraine what it needs

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.762
to help push them out.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.164
And that will help convince them

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.932
to leave on their own.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.501
And then finally, I think that NATO's

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.703
needs to recognize

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:59.239
that all of this depends

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.441
you know, all of this future

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.675
the future of European

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.777
security depends upon Europe.

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:07.213
Ukraine being secure in the future

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:11.050
so that if Russia is left on its own,

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.318
it will regroup.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.886
It will attack again.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.722
This will be a threat to all of Europe,

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.123
not only Ukraine.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:20.093
So as NATO's convenes in Vilnius, July of

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.361
the 12th,

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:23.630
they need to send

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.397
a signal

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:24.998
that Ukraine

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.399
is on the way into membership.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.501
So we'll get to that in a second.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.869
But I'm really interested to hear

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:30.503
what you say,

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.704
that they should give Ukraine

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.072
what it needs.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.507
A lot of the narrative

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.009
about the West, particularly

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.377
the United States

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:40.146
method of delivering weapons,

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.181
has been to do enough,

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.917
but not too much to antagonize Putin and

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.121
prompt some irrational response.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.189
Are you basically saying now

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.257
that that equation

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.492
should be out of the door

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.927
because you've seen a weakness in Russia?

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:58.731
Well, my own view, Christiane,

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.833
is that that is a wrong calculation.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.903
That's the boiling the frog argument

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.738
that we've gone slowly.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.940
We've increased, but we haven't provoked.

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:09.642
My view on

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.143
that is

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.645
if Putin could have done more already,

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:15.214
he would have already done it,

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.550
that he's not in this war in Ukraine

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.619
to lose. He's in it to win.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.754
And if he could add more troops,

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.556
if he could attack somewhere else,

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.391
if he thought that attacking and NATO's

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.826
ally would help him,

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.328
he would have done it.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.796
The fact is that he knows

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:32.098
he is losing in Ukraine.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.533
He can't possibly open

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:35.368
another front somewhere else.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.603
Least of all with the narrow country.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.472
He couldn't possibly handle that.

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:42.075
Nuclear weapons won't solve his problem.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:44.010
And I think he knows that

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.679
So he is putting these messages out

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:48.381
to deter us

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:49.649
rather than

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.084
to actually mean that he's

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:53.386
going to go in these various directions.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:54.721
We ought to understand that

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:55.621
we should be pouring

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.823
all the support to Ukraine.

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.991
Now, it's going to be really interesting

00:05:58.991 --> 00:05:59.425
to see

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:03.363
whether other leaders actually do this

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:05.064
because many have said that

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:07.967
had it been a lot more a lot earlier,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.036
we might already have seen a major

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.239
change on the battlefield.

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.842
But let me ask you, because, look,

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:18.211
there are those who say that

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.812
what happened over the weekend

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.547
and I think you said it as well.

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:25.284
Basically burst popped the Putin bubble.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:28.521
Others might think that actually,

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:29.722
you know, it's Prigozhin

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.290
that's on the run is the Wagner

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.425
people who turned around

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:36.362
and Putin is still pretty much in charge.

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.398
I want to play this byte,

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:39.198
part of an interview

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.134
from Secretary Blinken,

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:42.402
because it relates to this

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:44.070
and we'll talk about it

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:48.174
The fact that you have from within

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:49.542
someone directly questioning

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:50.610
Putin's authority,

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:51.144
directly

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:53.212
questioning the premises that upon

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:54.914
which he launched this aggression.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:56.015
Against Ukraine.

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.518
That in and of itself is something very,

00:06:58.684 --> 00:06:59.552
very powerful.

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.421
It adds cracks

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.556
where those go when they get there.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.291
Too soon to say

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.993
But it clearly raises new questions

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:07.960
that Putin has to deal with.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.263
So, Ambassador Volker,

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:11.764
clearly there was a lot of wishful

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.299
thinking over the weekend

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.367
and a certain

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:16.135
a certain amount of disappointment

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.036
from the

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:18.838
from the cognizant, if you like,

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.907
when Prigozhin turned round.

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.009
Do you what do you think?

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:23.409
I mean.

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:25.678
It's very Byzantine These are two

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.247
essential gangsters

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:29.315
fighting for

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:31.818
supremacy and money and power.

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:35.288
What do you think is Putin stronger

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:37.657
because he survived all the opposite,

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:40.193
because he's been challenged

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.895
Christiane, I think you asked exactly the

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:43.529
right question

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.064
because you framed it in the in

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:47.433
the sense of these are gangsters.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.102
This is a mafia mentality

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.637
that we're looking at.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.806
Putin can not live

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:56.676
with having been challenged this way.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.346
It is a threat to his control of Russia.

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.148
To his legitimacy

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:04.083
if he is seen to be weak.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:05.751
So he has no choice now

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:08.054
but to go after Prigozhin.

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:10.890
I think Prigozhin knew this knows this.

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:14.160
He stood down to position himself

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.496
as the reasonable person,

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:17.163
the one who doesn't

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:18.898
want to destroy the state.

00:08:18.898 --> 00:08:20.399
But then if Putin goes after him,

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.768
it gives him a justification

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:24.504
for trying again,

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:26.339
for somehow pushing back again.

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:28.608
So many shoes left to drop

00:08:28.608 --> 00:08:29.709
that we haven't seen

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.311
now as far as the U.S.

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:32.979
policy goes.

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:34.814
Again, I just want to come back to that.

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:35.648
The U.S.

00:08:35.648 --> 00:08:37.650
has no stake in this.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.051
Other than to say

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:40.786
get out of Ukraine,

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:43.789
live within your own borders and accept

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:45.625
responsibility for the war

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:46.993
that you launched.

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:48.461
Who runs Russia?

00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:49.962
There's no way we control

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:52.298
we control that. No way we can do that.

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:54.066
And we shouldn't pretend

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:55.201
that we're involved in that.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:56.702
So I think we've got that part of it

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:57.270
right.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:08:57.970
Okay.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:58.404
Very quick

00:08:58.404 --> 00:08:59.605
question about Putin

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:01.707
has also been at least certainly

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:02.975
the United States is concerned

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:04.810
that he's able to build up a

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.946
a coalition of those who support

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:08.047
in powerful countries

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:10.182
like China, to an extent, India,

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:13.419
you know, against the United States.

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:14.954
This is what the China

00:09:14.954 --> 00:09:16.789
Foreign Ministry said on the weekend.

00:09:16.789 --> 00:09:19.125
This is Russia's internal affair,

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:20.660
as Russia's friendly neighbor

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.495
and comprehensive strategic partner

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:24.564
of coordination for the new era.

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:26.198
China supports Russia

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:28.334
in maintaining national stability

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.570
and achieving development and prosperity.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.905
So they didn't use the name Putin.

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:33.306
And frankly,

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:34.273
they didn't put this out

00:09:34.273 --> 00:09:35.474
until it was clear

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:38.010
that the whatever it was was aborted

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:42.014
on the biggest strategic level.

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:44.850
How is this going to affect

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:46.652
Well, those people

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.621
who have suggested that

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:50.222
China is a strategic

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:52.792
ally of Russia and is helping Russia,

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:55.895
I think have misread the tea leaves here.

00:09:55.895 --> 00:09:58.364
China is very happy for Russia

00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:00.199
to try to weaken the West.

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:02.301
They can get anything from Russia

00:10:02.301 --> 00:10:03.869
that they want for cash,

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:05.004
whether it's minerals

00:10:05.004 --> 00:10:07.340
or whether it's energy, oil, gas, etc.

00:10:07.707 --> 00:10:10.109
They're not invested in Putin's war.

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:11.677
And I think they actually

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:12.945
look down on Russia.

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:14.046
They don't have a lot of respect

00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:15.014
for Russia

00:10:15.014 --> 00:10:16.983
because they view it as a declining power

00:10:16.983 --> 00:10:18.751
that doesn't take care of the state, does

00:10:18.751 --> 00:10:20.353
take care of the people.

00:10:20.353 --> 00:10:22.455
China is very much the opposite of that.

00:10:22.455 --> 00:10:24.490
So I'm not at all surprised that China,

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.558
looking at this, says

00:10:25.558 --> 00:10:28.494
it's just one more mess, more chaos.

00:10:28.861 --> 00:10:30.463
Putin is not the strong leader

00:10:30.463 --> 00:10:31.764
that he pretends to be.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:33.132
And we're just going to sit this out

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:34.200
and watch

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.636
China has time on its side and Russia

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:37.603
to China

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:39.171
appears intemperate and desperate.

